        <mxCell id="v3Tol91V-TR1hirwzvUr-180" parent="1" style="swimlane;horizontal=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="The Game Factorio" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="250" width="370" x="870" y="1120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="v3Tol91V-TR1hirwzvUr-181" parent="v3Tol91V-TR1hirwzvUr-180" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontSize=14;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;&quot; id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-6a9190fd-7fff-2835-ede6-03561adc55a1&quot;&gt;In the game Factorio, you combine various products in &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; color: rgb(106, 168, 79);&quot;&gt;Assemblers &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;to create new products. These products have progressively more complex inputs that form a large tree. Ultimately you build a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(191, 144, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;Rocket &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;to leave the planet, winning the game&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;The puzzle is how to best deliver resources around the map. At scale things get complicated which is fun.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="350" x="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="v3Tol91V-TR1hirwzvUr-182" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;" value="" vertex="1">
